         <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,635.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DUPORT</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>AFRICAN TERMINAL</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DANGOTE</td>\n                <td>₦1,608.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL LAGOS</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>A.Y.M SHAFA</td>\n                <td>₦1,720.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>FYNEFIELD</td>\n                <td>₦1,700.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Dangote Refinery Exports 476,000MT of Refined Products in Nine Cargoes for August\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Dangote Petroleum Refinery exported 476,000 metric tonnes (MT) of refined petroleum products in nine cargoes in August. August export programme covered Fuel Oil, Jet A1, automotive gas oil (AGO) and premium motor spirit (PMS) The largest cargo was the 144,000MT Fuel Oil shipment aboard Nordic Breeze.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/dangote-refinery-exports-476000mt-of-refined-products-in-nine-cargoes-for-august\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    JUST IN: Iran Strikes Oil Tanker in Strait of Hormuz as Global Oil Supply Fears Intensify\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Iran has struck another oil tanker in the Strait of Hormuz. The United Arab Emirates accuses Tehran of targeting a vessel affiliated with Abu Dhabi National Oil Company (ADNOC) The UAE said the attack hit the ship’s hull but caused no injuries.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/just-in-iran-strikes-oil-tanker-in-strait-of-hormuz-as-global-oil-supply-fears-intensify\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Depot Prices Weekly Review: 10th–14th August 2026\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria’s downstream petroleum market recorded mixed depot price movements between Monday, August 10 and Friday, August 14, 2026. While some depots raised their prices, others reduced their rates or held steady. AGO recorded the strongest price movements during the week, particularly in Lagos and Warri, while PMS prices generally posted smaller adjustments.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/depot-prices-weekly-review-10th14th-august-2026\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    NUPRC Unveils Crude Swap Plan to Boost Supply, Cut Refinery Costs\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Nigerian Upstream Petroleum Regulatory Commission is working on a domestic crude oil and gas swap arrangement. The proposal is aimed at reducing supply costs and improving feedstock availability for local refineries. The proposed framework is expected to strengthen compliance with the Domestic Crude Supply Obligation.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nuprc-unveils-crude-swap-plan-to-boost-supply-cut-refinery-costs\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    PETROAN Backs Tinubu’s Refinery Push, Warns NNPCL Against Another Costly Failure\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria’s latest push to revive its state-owned refineries must move beyond rehabilitation promises and commissioning ceremonies, the Petroleum Products Retail Outlets Owners Association of Nigeria has warned. PETROAN backed President Bola Tinubu's renewed commitment to restoring the Port Harcourt and Warri refineries, but said the initiative will only succeed if NNPC Ltd ties the proposed partnership to firm deadlines.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/petroan-backs-tinubus-refinery-push-warns-nnpcl-against-another-costly-failure\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
